From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 01:45:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add GalaxyCore GC2083 sensor driver

Add a V4L2 driver for the GalaxyCore GC2083, a 1920x1080 RAW10 sensor
with a two-lane MIPI CSI-2 output. Milk-V sells it as the CAM-GC2083
module for the Duo and Duo S.

The register table comes from Sophgo's duo-buildroot-sdk-v2, which has
no license. Ingenic's GPL-2.0+ gc2083.c (themactep/ingenic-sdk,
common/sensor/t31) has the same table for a 27 MHz MCLK, apart from the
PLL, frame timing and analogue settings.

Supported: 1920x1080 at 30 fps with a 24 MHz MCLK, or at 29.7 fps with
23.76 MHz.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
